        id: 'cranio-2',
        title: 'Types of Craniosynostosis',
        content: `## Classification of Craniosynostosis

### Single Suture Synostosis

**Sagittal Synostosis (Scaphocephaly):**
- Most common (40-55%)
- Elongated, narrow skull (dolichocephalic)
- Frontal bossing, occipital protrusion
- Palpable ridge along sagittal suture

**Metopic Synostosis (Trigonocephaly):**
- Triangular forehead
- Hypotelorism
- Midline frontal ridge
- May be subtle

**Unilateral Coronal (Anterior Plagiocephaly):**
- Flattened forehead on affected side
- Elevated superior orbital rim
- Harlequin eye deformity
- Deviated nasal root

**Bilateral Coronal (Brachycephaly):**
- Short, wide skull
- Flattened forehead
- Bilateral orbital changes
- Often syndromic

**Lambdoid Synostosis (Posterior Plagiocephaly):**
- Rare (1-3% of synostoses)
- Flattened occiput, bulging mastoid
- Must differentiate from positional

### Syndromic vs Non-Syndromic

| Feature | Non-Syndromic | Syndromic |
|---------|---------------|-----------|
| Sutures involved | Usually single | Often multiple |
| Family history | Rare | Often positive |
| Associated anomalies | No | Yes (limbs, face) |
| Genetic testing | Usually negative | FGFR mutations common |

### Positional Plagiocephaly

**NOT Craniosynostosis:**
- Open sutures
- Due to external pressure (supine sleeping)
- Parallelogram head shape
- Ear position shifted forward on flat side
- Frontal bossing same side

**Differentiation from Lambdoid Synostosis:**

| Feature | Positional | Lambdoid Synostosis |
|---------|------------|---------------------|
| Head shape | Parallelogram | Trapezoid |
| Ear position | Anterior on flat side | Posterior/inferior on flat side |
| Mastoid | Normal | Bulging |
| Occipital ridge | Absent | Present |
| Skull base | Level | Tilted |`,
