        content: `## Surgical Techniques

### Dorsal Reduction

**Cartilaginous Dorsum:**
- Scalpel or scissors
- Direct visualization (open)
- Remove sequentially

**Bony Dorsum:**
- Rasp (conservative reduction)
- Osteotome (larger humps)
- Powered instrumentation

**Maintaining Middle Vault:**
- Spreader grafts
- Preservation of T-junction
- Prevent inverted-V deformity

### Osteotomies

**Purpose:**
- Narrow nasal bones
- Close open roof
- Straighten crooked nose

**Types:**

| Type | Location | Function |
|------|----------|----------|
| **Lateral** | Along piriform | Mobilize nasal bone |
| **Medial** | Paramedian | Complete mobilization |
| **Intermediate** | Mid-bone | Narrow wide bones |
| **Transverse** | Radix | Shorten nasal bones |

**Technique:**
- Percutaneous or intranasal
- Low-to-high direction
- 2mm osteotome
- Greenstick fracture at radix

### Spreader Grafts

**Indication:**
- Prevent/treat middle vault collapse
- Widen narrow internal valve
- Straighten crooked nose

**Technique:**
- Cartilage (septal, auricular)
- Place between ULC and septum
- 3-4mm x 20-25mm

### Tip Techniques

**Conservative (Suture):**
- Transdomal suture (narrow dome)
- Interdomal suture (narrow tip)
- Tip rotation suture
- Lateral crural steal

**Cartilage Modifying:**
- Cephalic trim (refine tip)
- Dome division
- Vertical dome division

**Grafts:**
| Graft | Purpose |
|-------|---------|
| **Columellar strut** | Tip support |
| **Shield/cap graft** | Tip definition |
| **Alar contour graft** | Alar retraction |
| **Lateral crural strut** | Lateral crural support |

### Cephalic Trim

**Technique:**
- Remove cephalic portion of LLC
- Preserve 6-8mm of complete strip
- Most common tip refinement technique

**Complications:**
- Over-resection → Pinching, collapse
- Asymmetry
- Loss of support`,
