          'Facial aging: Bone resorption + fat descent/deflation + ligament laxity + skin changes',
          'SMAS: Superficial Musculoaponeurotic System - continuous with platysma and frontalis; key to durable lift',
          'Retaining ligaments (zygomatic, mandibular) must be released for adequate tissue mobilization',
          'Great auricular nerve: Most commonly injured nerve in facelift - 6.5cm below tragus over SCM',
          'Facial layers: Skin → Subcutaneous fat → SMAS/Platysma → Deep fascia → Muscles → Bone',
          'Fat compartments: Superficial (nasolabial, malar, jowl) and Deep (SOOF, buccal, deep malar)',
          'Danger zones: Temporal branch over zygoma, marginal mandibular below mandible',
          'McGregor\'s patch: Zygomatic ligament that must be released for malar elevation'
