        id: 'lipo-4',
        title: 'Body Contouring and HD Liposuction',
        content: `## Advanced Techniques

### High-Definition Liposuction

**Concept:**
- Athletic, sculpted appearance
- Highlight muscle definition
- Superficial fat removal

**Targets:**
- Abdominal etching (six-pack)
- Pectoralis definition
- Arm definition
- Back definition

**Requirements:**
- Fit patient with muscle development
- Good skin quality
- VASER typically used
- Surgeon artistic skill

**Technique:**
- Mark muscle borders
- Superficial liposuction over muscle
- Deeper removal between muscles
- Create shadows and highlights

### Fat Grafting After Liposuction

**Autologous Transfer:**
- Harvest with liposuction
- Process fat
- Reinject to desired areas

**Common Transfers:**
- Brazilian Butt Lift (BBL)
- Breast fat grafting
- Facial fat grafting

### Brazilian Butt Lift

**Technique:**
- Liposuction donor areas
- Process fat
- Inject into buttocks

**CRITICAL SAFETY:**
- **SUBCUTANEOUS ONLY**
- NEVER inject into muscle
- Avoid gluteal veins
- Cannula tip visible/superficial

**Mortality:**
- Highest of aesthetic procedures
- Death from fat embolism
- Deep injection → gluteal vein entry

### Liposuction Combined Procedures

**With Abdominoplasty:**
- Limited undermining
- Preserve lateral perforators
- Or stage procedures

**With Other Procedures:**
- Limit total procedure time
- Consider staging
- Cumulative risk

### Post-Operative Care

**Compression Garments:**
- Continuous wear 4-6 weeks
- Reduces swelling and ecchymosis
- Improves skin retraction

**Activity:**
- Early ambulation (VTE prevention)
- Restrict strenuous activity 2-4 weeks
- Gradual return to exercise

**Results Timeline:**
- Immediate: Swelling obscures
- 4-6 weeks: Swelling decreasing
- 3-6 months: Final result
- Up to 12 months for full skin retraction`,
