        content: `## Craniosynostosis Types

### Sagittal Synostosis (Scaphocephaly)

**Appearance:**
- Elongated skull (boat-shaped)
- ↑ AP diameter
- ↓ Biparietal diameter
- Frontal bossing
- Occipital protrusion

**Cephalic Index:**
- CI = (Width/Length) × 100
- Normal: 76-80
- Scaphocephaly: <70

### Coronal Synostosis

**Unilateral (Plagiocephaly):**
- Flattened forehead on affected side
- Elevated orbit (harlequin deformity)
- Nasal deviation to affected side
- Contralateral frontal bossing

**Bilateral (Brachycephaly):**
- Short AP dimension
- Wide skull
- Flat forehead
- Turricephaly (tower skull) possible

### Metopic Synostosis (Trigonocephaly)

**Appearance:**
- Triangular forehead
- Palpable midline ridge
- Hypotelorism
- Upslanting palpebral fissures

### Lambdoid Synostosis (Posterior Plagiocephaly)

**Appearance:**
- Flattened occiput on affected side
- Mastoid displaced posteriorly
- Ipsilateral ear posterior and inferior

**vs Positional Plagiocephaly:**
| Feature | Lambdoid Synostosis | Positional |
|---------|---------------------|------------|
| Ear position | Posterior/inferior | Anterior |
| Mastoid | Posteriorly displaced | Normal |
| Incidence | Rare (1-3%) | Common |
| Suture on CT | Fused | Open |

### Diagnosis

**Physical Exam:**
- Head shape assessment
- Palpation of sutures
- Measure head circumference
- Fontanelle assessment

**Imaging:**
- CT with 3D reconstruction (gold standard)
- Plain radiographs (screening)
- MRI (brain assessment)

**When to Suspect ICP Elevation:**
- Bulging fontanelle
- Papilledema
- Headache, irritability
- Developmental delay`,
