        id: 'mast-1',
        title: 'Ptosis Classification',
        content: `## Breast Ptosis Assessment

### Definition

**Ptosis:** Descent of the nipple-areola complex (NAC) relative to the inframammary fold (IMF)

### Regnault Classification

| Grade | Description |
|-------|-------------|
| **I (Mild)** | NAC at IMF level |
| **II (Moderate)** | NAC below IMF but above lower pole |
| **III (Severe)** | NAC at lowest point of breast |
| **Pseudoptosis** | NAC above IMF, parenchyma below |
| **Parenchymal maldistribution** | NAC in normal position, inferior pole empty |

### Anatomic Reference Points

**Normal Breast:**
- NAC: 21-23 cm from sternal notch
- NAC: 9-11 cm from midclavicular point
- NAC: Above IMF
- IMF: 5-8 cm below NAC

### Etiology of Ptosis

**Causes:**
- Pregnancy/breastfeeding
- Weight fluctuation
- Aging and gravity
- Breast involution
- Congenital hypoplasia

### Clinical Assessment

**Measurements:**
| Parameter | Normal |
|-----------|--------|
| SN to N | 19-23 cm |
| N to IMF | 5-8 cm |
| IMF to IMF | Variable |
| Base width | 10-14 cm |

**Evaluate:**
- Degree of ptosis
- Skin quality/elasticity
- Breast volume
- Asymmetry
- Goals (with/without implant)

### Surgery Selection

**Based on Ptosis Degree:**
| Ptosis | Procedure |
|--------|-----------|
| Pseudoptosis | Augmentation or periareolar |
| Grade I | Periareolar or vertical |
| Grade II | Vertical or Wise pattern |
| Grade III | Wise pattern (anchor) |

### Augmentation-Mastopexy

**Combined Procedure:**
- Higher revision rate
- Competing goals
- May stage if complex`,
