        id: 'pedhand-1',
        title: 'Classification Systems',
        content: `## Congenital Hand Differences

### OMT Classification (Swanson Modified)

**Original Oberg-Manske-Tonkin Classification:**

| Category | Description | Examples |
|----------|-------------|----------|
| **I** | Failure of formation | Transverse (amelia), Longitudinal (radial club) |
| **II** | Failure of differentiation | Syndactyly, camptodactyly |
| **III** | Duplication | Polydactyly |
| **IV** | Overgrowth | Macrodactyly |
| **V** | Undergrowth | Brachydactyly, thumb hypoplasia |
| **VI** | Constriction band | Amniotic band syndrome |
| **VII** | Generalized skeletal abnormalities | Syndromes |

### Incidence

**Most Common:**
1. Syndactyly
2. Polydactyly
3. Camptodactyly

### Embryology

**Critical Period:**
- Limb bud: Day 26-28
- Complete hand: Week 8
- Critical period: Weeks 4-8

**Signaling Centers:**
- Zone of Polarizing Activity (ZPA): Radial-ulnar axis (SHH)
- Apical Ectodermal Ridge (AER): Proximal-distal (FGFs)
- Dorsal ectoderm: Dorsal-ventral (Wnt-7a)

### Syndromes

**Associated Syndromes:**
| Syndrome | Hand Finding |
|----------|--------------|
| Apert | Syndactyly (mitten hand) |
| Poland | Absent pectoralis, brachydactyly |
| Holt-Oram | Radial deficiency |
| VACTERL | Various |
| TAR | Thrombocytopenia, absent radius |

### Timing of Surgery

**General Guidelines:**
| Age | Intervention |
|-----|--------------|
| 3-6 months | Thumb reconstruction |
| 6-12 months | Syndactyly release |
| 1-2 years | Many other procedures |
| 4-6 years | Toe transfers |

### Evaluation

**Assessment:**
- Complete hand examination
- Range of motion
- Grip and pinch
- Family history
- Associated anomalies (cardiac, renal)`,
