        id: 'pedhand-4',
        title: 'Other Congenital Hand Conditions',
        content: `## Additional Conditions

### Camptodactyly

**Definition:**
- Flexion contracture of PIP joint
- Usually small finger
- Progressive

**Treatment:**
- Splinting first
- Surgery if severe (>40-60°)
- Results variable

### Clinodactyly

**Definition:**
- Angular deviation of digit
- Usually radial deviation of small finger
- Delta phalanx (triangular bone)

**Treatment:**
- Observation if mild
- Opening wedge osteotomy if severe

### Trigger Thumb

**Pediatric Trigger Thumb:**
- Notta's nodule (thickened FPL)
- Locked in flexion
- NOT CONGENITAL (develops postnatally)

**Treatment:**
- Observation: May resolve (30%)
- Surgery: Release A1 pulley if persistent
- Timing: After 1 year if not resolved

### Radial Longitudinal Deficiency (Radial Club Hand)

**Classification:**

| Type | Description |
|------|-------------|
| I | Short radius |
| II | Hypoplastic radius |
| III | Partial absence |
| IV | Complete absence |

**Associated:**
- TAR syndrome
- Holt-Oram syndrome
- VACTERL association

**Treatment:**
- Stretching, splinting
- Centralization or radialization
- Thumb reconstruction

### Cleft Hand (Ectrodactyly)

**Features:**
- Absence of central rays
- "Lobster claw" appearance
- V-shaped cleft
- Often syndactyly of remaining digits

**Treatment:**
- Cleft closure (Snow-Littler)
- Syndactyly release
- First web deepening

### Macrodactyly

**Definition:**
- Enlargement of digit(s)
- True macrodactyly: Nerve territory
- Often median nerve distribution

**Treatment:**
- Debulking procedures
- Epiphysiodesis
- Ray amputation if severe

### Constriction Band Syndrome

**Features:**
- Circumferential bands
- Distal lymphedema
- Acrosyndactyly
- Amputation

**Treatment:**
- Band release (Z-plasty)
- Urgent if vascular compromise
- Syndactyly release
- Web reconstruction`,
