        id: 'flex-1',
        title: 'Anatomy and Zones',
        content: `## Flexor Tendon Anatomy

### Flexor Tendons of the Hand

**Extrinsic Flexors:**
- Flexor Digitorum Superficialis (FDS)
- Flexor Digitorum Profundus (FDP)
- Flexor Pollicis Longus (FPL)

**FDS:**
- Originates: Medial epicondyle, radius, ulna
- Inserts: Middle phalanx base
- Splits (Camper's chiasma) to allow FDP through

**FDP:**
- Originates: Ulna, interosseous membrane
- Inserts: Distal phalanx base
- Passes through FDS split

### Pulley System

**Annular Pulleys (A1-A5):**
| Pulley | Location | Critical? |
|--------|----------|-----------|
| A1 | MCP joint | No (can release) |
| **A2** | Proximal phalanx | **YES - preserve** |
| A3 | PIP joint | No |
| **A4** | Middle phalanx | **YES - preserve** |
| A5 | DIP joint | No |

**Cruciate Pulleys (C1-C3):**
- Between annular pulleys
- Allow flexibility

**Critical Pulleys:**
- A2 and A4 must be preserved
- Loss = bowstringing

### Flexor Zones (Verdan)

| Zone | Location | Notes |
|------|----------|-------|
| **I** | FDP only (distal to FDS) | Single tendon |
| **II** | Flexor sheath (A1-FDS insertion) | "No man's land" |
| **III** | Palm (carpal tunnel to A1) | Lumbrical origin |
| **IV** | Carpal tunnel | Tight space |
| **V** | Forearm (proximal to tunnel) | Muscle belly |

**Zone II ("No Man's Land"):**
- Two tendons in tight sheath
- Historically poor results
- Now repairable with modern techniques

### Thumb Zones

| Zone | Location |
|------|----------|
| T-I | FPL insertion to IP |
| T-II | A1 pulley to IP |
| T-III | Thenar eminence |

### Blood Supply

**Vincular System:**
- Vincula brevia and longa
- Blood supply to tendons
- From digital vessels

**Nutrition:**
- Vascular (vincular)
- Synovial diffusion`,
