        id: 'ext-1',
        title: 'Extensor Anatomy and Zones',
        content: `## Extensor Tendon Anatomy

### Extrinsic Extensors

**Wrist Extensors:**
- ECRL (Extensor Carpi Radialis Longus)
- ECRB (Extensor Carpi Radialis Brevis)
- ECU (Extensor Carpi Ulnaris)

**Finger Extensors:**
- EDC (Extensor Digitorum Communis)
- EIP (Extensor Indicis Proprius)
- EDM (Extensor Digiti Minimi)

**Thumb:**
- EPL (Extensor Pollicis Longus)
- EPB (Extensor Pollicis Brevis)
- APL (Abductor Pollicis Longus)

### Extensor Apparatus

**Components:**
- Central slip (to middle phalanx)
- Lateral bands (to distal phalanx)
- Sagittal bands (at MCP)
- Triangular ligament (distally)

### Dorsal Compartments

**6 Extensor Compartments:**
| Compartment | Contents |
|-------------|----------|
| 1 | APL, EPB |
| 2 | ECRL, ECRB |
| 3 | EPL |
| 4 | EDC, EIP |
| 5 | EDM |
| 6 | ECU |

**Lister's Tubercle:** Between 2 and 3

### Extensor Zones (Verdan)

**Odd Numbers = Joints:**
| Zone | Location |
|------|----------|
| I | DIP joint |
| II | Middle phalanx |
| III | PIP joint |
| IV | Proximal phalanx |
| V | MCP joint |
| VI | Metacarpal |
| VII | Wrist |
| VIII | Forearm |

**Thumb Zones (T):**
| Zone | Location |
|------|----------|
| T-I | IP joint |
| T-II | Proximal phalanx |
| T-III | MCP joint |
| T-IV | Metacarpal |
| T-V | Wrist |

### Juncturae Tendinum

**Connection between EDC tendons:**
- Allows extension even with EDC laceration
- May mask complete tendon injury`,
