        id: 'bred-1',
        title: 'Patient Evaluation',
        content: `## Breast Reduction Assessment

### Indications

**Symptomatic Macromastia:**
- Neck pain
- Back pain
- Shoulder grooving
- Intertrigo under breasts
- Posture problems
- Activity limitation

**Psychological:**
- Self-consciousness
- Difficulty finding clothes
- Quality of life impact

### History

**Essential History:**
- Weight history (stable?)
- Prior breast surgery
- Family history (cancer)
- Smoking status
- Medications (anticoagulants)
- Future pregnancy plans
- Breastfeeding desire

### Physical Examination

**Measurements:**
| Measurement | Description |
|-------------|-------------|
| SN-N | Sternal notch to nipple |
| N-IMF | Nipple to inframammary fold |
| Base width | Breast base diameter |
| Ptosis grade | Nipple position vs IMF |

**Ptosis Classification (Regnault):**
| Grade | Nipple Position |
|-------|-----------------|
| I | At IMF level |
| II | Below IMF, above lower pole |
| III | At lowest pole, points down |
| Pseudo | Gland below fold, nipple above |

### Preoperative Planning

**Imaging:**
- Mammogram if age-appropriate
- Baseline for future screening

**Photography:**
- Standard views
- Document asymmetry

### Markings

**Key Points:**
- Sternal midline
- Breast meridian
- New nipple position (18-22 cm from SN)
- Inframammary fold
- Keyhole or Wise pattern

**New Nipple Position:**
- Usually at IMF level or 1-2 cm above
- 18-22 cm from sternal notch
- On breast meridian

### Insurance Considerations

**Schnur Scale:**
- BSA-based weight thresholds
- Documents medical necessity
- Required for coverage`,
