        id: 'hair-1',
        title: 'Hair Biology and Classification',
        content: `## Hair Biology and Pattern Baldness

### Hair Cycle

**Phases:**
| Phase | Duration | Description |
|-------|----------|-------------|
| Anagen | 2-6 years | Active growth |
| Catagen | 2-3 weeks | Transition |
| Telogen | 2-3 months | Resting/shedding |

**Scalp Hair:**
- 85-90% in anagen
- 100,000 average hairs
- Grows ~0.35 mm/day

### Follicular Unit

**Definition:**
- Natural grouping of 1-4 hairs
- With sebaceous glands
- Arrector pili muscle
- Neurovascular supply

**Types:**
- 1-hair FU: Hairline
- 2-3 hair FU: Mid-scalp
- 4-hair FU: Crown, dense areas

### Androgenetic Alopecia

**Male Pattern Baldness:**
- DHT-mediated
- Genetically programmed
- Progressive miniaturization

**Pathophysiology:**
- 5-alpha reductase converts testosterone to DHT
- DHT binds androgen receptors
- Hair follicle miniaturization
- Terminal → vellus hair

### Norwood Classification (Male)

| Class | Pattern |
|-------|---------|
| I | Minimal recession |
| II | Triangular frontotemporal |
| III | Deep frontotemporal |
| III vertex | Crown involvement |
| IV | Frontal + crown, band between |
| V | Band narrowing |
| VI | Band lost |
| VII | Extensive, only occipital rim |

### Ludwig Classification (Female)

| Grade | Description |
|-------|-------------|
| I | Widening of central part |
| II | Diffuse thinning crown |
| III | Extensive central thinning |

### Donor Dominance

**Key Principle:**
- Transplanted hair retains donor characteristics
- Occipital hair = DHT resistant
- Maintains characteristics at recipient site
- "Safe donor zone" (occipital/temporal)`,
