        title: 'Post-operative Care and Results',
        content: `## Post-op Care and Timeline

### Immediate Post-op

**First 24-48 hours:**
- Keep grafts moist (saline spray)
- Sleep elevated
- Avoid touching grafts
- Gentle shampooing day 2-3

### Healing Timeline

| Time | Phase |
|------|-------|
| Day 1-3 | Crusting around grafts |
| Week 1 | Crusts fall off |
| Week 2-3 | "Shock loss" begins |
| Month 1-3 | Grafts in telogen |
| Month 3-4 | New growth begins |
| Month 6 | Noticeable improvement |
| Month 12 | Near-final result |
| Month 18 | Final result |

### Shock Loss

**Definition:**
- Transplanted hairs shed
- Normal phenomenon
- Hairs enter telogen
- New growth at 3-4 months

**Reassurance:**
- Expected in most patients
- Follicle alive
- New hair will grow

### Medical Adjuncts

**Finasteride:**
- 5-alpha reductase inhibitor
- 1 mg daily
- Slows/stops progression
- May regrow some hair

**Minoxidil:**
- 2% or 5% topical
- Prolongs anagen
- Apply to thinning areas
- Continue long-term

**Low-Level Laser:**
- FDA-cleared devices
- May stimulate follicles
- Adjunct therapy

### Expected Results

**Graft Survival:** 90-95%

**Density:**
- Natural: 80-120 FU/cm²
- Transplant: 30-50 FU/cm²
- Multiple sessions may be needed

**Sessions Needed:**
- Mild: 1 session
- Moderate: 1-2 sessions
- Severe: 2-3+ sessions

### Limitations

**Finite Donor:**
- Limited safe donor zone
- ~5000-8000 FUs total
- Plan for lifetime needs

**Progressive Loss:**
- Native hair continues to thin
- May need medical therapy
- Future sessions possible`,
