        title: 'Hyaluronic Acid Fillers',
        content: `## Hyaluronic Acid Fillers

### HA Properties

**Benefits:**
- Natural tissue component
- Reversible (hyaluronidase)
- Hydrophilic
- Various viscosities

**Products:**
| Product | Uses | Duration |
|---------|------|----------|
| Juvederm Ultra | Lips, NLF | 6-12 mo |
| Juvederm Voluma | Cheeks | 12-24 mo |
| Restylane | NLF, lips | 6-12 mo |
| Belotero | Fine lines | 6-9 mo |

### Facial Anatomy for Filling

**Volume Restoration:**
- Temples
- Cheeks
- Tear troughs
- Nasolabial folds
- Marionette lines
- Jawline

**Enhancement:**
- Lips
- Chin
- Nose (non-surgical)

### Injection Techniques

**Methods:**
| Technique | Use |
|-----------|-----|
| Linear threading | NLF, marionettes |
| Serial puncture | Lips |
| Fanning | Cheeks |
| Bolus/depot | Deep volume |
| Cannula | Larger areas, safety |

**Planes:**
- Subcutaneous
- Supraperiosteal (deep)
- Intradermal (fine lines)

### Danger Zones

**Vascular Occlusion Risk:**

| Area | At-Risk Vessel |
|------|----------------|
| Glabella | Supratrochlear |
| Nose | Angular, dorsal nasal |
| Nasolabial fold | Angular artery |
| Lips | Superior/inferior labial |

**Prevention:**
- Know anatomy
- Aspirate before injecting
- Low pressure, slow injection
- Consider cannula

### Hyaluronidase

**Enzyme that dissolves HA:**
- Dose: 10-75 units per area
- Quick action
- May need repeat
- Allergic potential

**Indications:**
- Vascular compromise
- Overcorrection
- Migration
- Nodules`,
