        content: `## Non-HA Fillers

### Calcium Hydroxylapatite (Radiesse)

**Properties:**
- CaHA microspheres in gel
- Stimulates collagen
- Longer lasting (12-18 mo)
- NOT reversible

**Uses:**
- Deep NLF
- Cheeks
- Hands
- Jaw

**Contraindications:**
- Lips (nodules)
- Periorbital (visible)

### Poly-L-Lactic Acid (Sculptra)

**Biostimulator:**
- Stimulates collagen production
- Gradual results
- Long-lasting (2+ years)
- Multiple sessions needed

**Technique:**
- Reconstitute 24+ hours before
- Deep injection
- Massage after injection
- "5-5-5 rule" (massage)

**Complications:**
- Nodules (superficial injection)
- Papules

### Polymethylmethacrylate (Bellafill)

**Permanent Filler:**
- PMMA microspheres
- Bovine collagen carrier
- Skin test required
- FDA approved for acne scars

**Risks:**
- Granuloma
- Infection
- Permanent issues

### Autologous Fat

**Properties:**
- Natural
- Long-lasting if engrafted
- Variable retention (30-70%)
- Overfilling needed

**Technique:**
- Harvest from donor site
- Process (wash, centrifuge)
- Inject in multiple passes
- Avoid large boluses

### Comparison

| Filler | Duration | Reversible |
|--------|----------|------------|
| HA | 6-24 mo | Yes |
| CaHA | 12-18 mo | No |
| PLLA | 2+ years | No |
| PMMA | Permanent | No |
| Fat | Variable | No |`,
