        id: 'ortho-1',
        title: 'Evaluation and Planning',
        content: `## Orthognathic Surgery Evaluation

### Indications

**Dentofacial Deformities:**
- Skeletal malocclusion
- Facial asymmetry
- Sleep apnea (skeletal)
- TMJ dysfunction
- Trauma sequelae

### Clinical Examination

**Facial Analysis:**
- Frontal view: Symmetry, proportions
- Profile view: Jaw relationships
- Three-quarter view: Cheek projection

**Dental Analysis:**
- Angle classification
- Overjet and overbite
- Transverse relationship
- Dental midlines

### Angle Classification

| Class | Description |
|-------|-------------|
| I | Normal molar relationship |
| II | Mandible retrusive (div 1 or 2) |
| III | Mandible protrusive |

**Division:**
- II div 1: Proclined incisors
- II div 2: Retroclined incisors

### Cephalometric Analysis

**Key Measurements:**
| Angle | Normal | Meaning |
|-------|--------|---------|
| SNA | 82° | Maxilla to skull base |
| SNB | 80° | Mandible to skull base |
| ANB | 2° | Maxilla-mandible relationship |
| FMA | 25° | Mandibular plane angle |

**Positive ANB:** Skeletal Class II
**Negative ANB:** Skeletal Class III

### Planning

**Virtual Surgical Planning:**
- 3D CT imaging
- Computer planning
- Surgical guides
- Precise movements

**Model Surgery:**
- Traditional method
- Dental models
- Face bow transfer
- Articulator mounting

### Team Approach

**Collaboration:**
- Oral/Maxillofacial surgeon
- Orthodontist
- Sometimes: ENT, speech therapy

**Sequence:**
1. Pre-surgical orthodontics (decompensation)
2. Surgery
3. Post-surgical orthodontics (finishing)`,
