        title: 'Extremity and Breast',
        content: `## Arm, Thigh, and Breast Procedures

### Brachioplasty

**Goals:**
- Remove excess arm skin
- Contour arm
- Improve function

**Technique:**
- Medial arm incision
- Bicipital groove to axilla
- May extend to chest wall (axillary brachioplasty)

**Scar Location:**
- Visible scar trade-off
- Discuss extensively with patient

**Complications:**
- Visible scar
- Lymphedema
- Seroma
- Wound issues

### Thigh Lift

**Options:**
| Type | Indication |
|------|------------|
| Medial | Inner thigh laxity |
| Vertical | Significant laxity |
| Spiral | Circumferential |

**Medial Thigh Lift:**
- Crease incision (groin)
- Limited correction
- Scar migration

**Vertical Thigh Lift:**
- Medial thigh incision
- Greater correction
- Visible scar

**Spiral Thigh Lift:**
- Combined with buttock lift
- Comprehensive lower body

### Breast Procedures

**Post-MWL Breasts:**
- Severe ptosis
- Volume loss
- Skin excess

**Female:**
- Breast lift (mastopexy)
- Often with augmentation
- Auto-augmentation techniques

**Male (Gynecomastia):**
- Skin/gland excision
- Similar to post-MWL chest

### Combination Procedures

**Staging Options:**
- All at once (high risk)
- Two stages: Upper + Lower
- Serial procedures

**Common Combinations:**
- Lower body lift + brachioplasty
- Breast + abdomen
- Upper body lift

### Complications Specific

**Arms:**
- Medial wound tension
- Lymphedema risk
- Scar widening

**Thighs:**
- Scar migration downward
- Labial distortion
- Wound issues`,
