        id: 'mwl-4',
        title: 'Complications and Special Considerations',
        content: `## Special Considerations

### Unique Challenges in MWL

**Poor Tissue Quality:**
- Inelastic skin
- Minimal fat layer
- Poor blood supply
- Prone to wound issues

**Nutritional:**
- Protein deficiency → poor healing
- Vitamin deficiency
- Anemia
- Supplement before surgery

### DVT Prevention

**High Risk Population:**

**Prevention Protocol:**
- Ambulate early
- SCDs intraoperatively
- Chemical prophylaxis
- Extended prophylaxis (2-4 weeks)

### Wound Healing

**Common Issues:**
- Dehiscence at tension points
- Skin necrosis
- Seroma

**Prevention:**
- Quilting sutures
- Progressive tension closure
- Drains
- Avoid tension
- Optimize nutrition

### Staging Strategies

**Two-Stage Approach:**

| Stage | Procedures |
|-------|------------|
| 1 | Lower body lift, abdomen |
| 2 | Arms, breasts, face |

**Timing:**
- 3-6 months between stages
- Allow full recovery

### Revision Surgery

**Common Needs:**
- Scar revision
- Dog ear excision
- Further tissue removal
- Touch-up procedures

**Rate:** 20-40% may need revision

### Psychological Aspects

**Body Image:**
- May not match expectations
- Scars are trade-off
- Pre-op counseling important

**Realistic Expectations:**
- Improvement, not perfection
- Scars are permanent
- May need revisions`,
