        content: `## Medical Photography Principles

### Importance

**Clinical Documentation:**
- Medical-legal record
- Pre/post comparison
- Communication
- Teaching/publication
- Insurance documentation

### Standards

**Consistency:**
- Same background
- Same lighting
- Same positioning
- Same distance
- Same camera settings

**Essential Elements:**
- Neutral background (blue/gray)
- Even lighting (minimal shadows)
- Appropriate framing
- Proper exposure

### Camera Equipment

**Requirements:**
| Feature | Recommended |
|---------|-------------|
| Camera | DSLR or mirrorless |
| Sensor | Full-frame or APS-C |
| Lens | 85-105mm (portrait) |
| Flash | Ring flash or dual strobe |

**Settings:**
- Aperture: f/8-f/11
- ISO: Low (100-400)
- Shutter: 1/60-1/125
- WB: Flash or custom

### Lighting

**Goals:**
- Even illumination
- Minimal shadows
- Color accuracy
- Highlight contours

**Options:**
- Ring flash (even)
- Dual strobes (modeling)
- Continuous lights

### Background

**Standard:**
- Neutral color (18% gray or light blue)
- Non-reflective
- Smooth, uncluttered

### Patient Preparation

**Guidelines:**
- Remove jewelry
- Hair pulled back (face)
- Minimal/no makeup
- Standard positioning
- Relaxed, neutral expression`,
