        content: `## Bite Injuries and Special Infections

### Human Bite (Fight Bite)

**Mechanism:**
- Punch to mouth
- Tooth penetrates MCP joint
- Often small wound

**Organisms:**
- Eikenella corrodens
- Streptococcus
- Staph aureus
- Oral anaerobes

**High Suspicion:**
- Any wound over MCP
- Small laceration
- "Punched a wall" story

**Treatment:**
- Assume joint penetration
- Surgical exploration and irrigation
- IV antibiotics (Augmentin or ampicillin-sulbactam)
- Leave wound open
- Splint and elevate

### Animal Bites

**Cat Bites:**
- Deep puncture wounds
- High infection rate (50%)
- Pasteurella multocida
- May need operative I&D

**Dog Bites:**
- Crush injury pattern
- Pasteurella, Staph, Strep
- Lower infection rate than cat
- Copious irrigation

**Treatment:**
- Irrigation
- Debridement if needed
- Augmentin (covers Pasteurella)
- Tetanus and rabies prophylaxis

### Osteomyelitis

**Presentation:**
- Chronic wound/drainage
- Pain out of proportion
- May be indolent

**Diagnosis:**
- X-ray: Late changes
- MRI: More sensitive
- Bone biopsy: Gold standard

**Treatment:**
- Surgical debridement
- 6 weeks IV antibiotics
- May need flap coverage

### Atypical Infections

| Organism | Setting | Treatment |
|----------|---------|-----------|
| Mycobacterium marinum | Fish tanks, aquariums | Clarithromycin + ethambutol |
| Sporotrichosis | Gardening (roses) | Itraconazole |
| Nocardia | Soil exposure | TMP-SMX |

**M. marinum:**
- Indolent nodules along lymphatics
- Fish tank granuloma
- Requires months of treatment`,
