        id: 'sga-2',
        title: 'Harvesting Techniques',
        content: `## Graft Harvesting Techniques

### STSG Harvest

**Instruments:**
| Device | Features |
|--------|----------|
| Weck blade | Freehand, small areas |
| Goulian | Adjustable, freehand |
| Dermatome (air/electric) | Precise, large areas |
| Zimmer | Electric dermatome |

**Technique:**
1. Lubricate (mineral oil)
2. Apply tension
3. Smooth, consistent stroke
4. Maintain angle

**Thickness:**
- Thin: 8-12/1000 inch
- Intermediate: 12-16/1000 inch
- Thick: 16-20/1000 inch

### Donor Sites

**STSG Common:**
- Thigh (anterolateral)
- Buttock (children)
- Scalp (good color match face)
- Back

**FTSG Common:**
- Groin
- Supraclavicular
- Preauricular/postauricular
- Upper eyelid
- Inner arm

### FTSG Harvest

**Technique:**
1. Design template
2. Excise skin
3. Defat graft (remove fat)
4. Primary closure donor site

**Critical:**
- Complete defatting
- Fat prevents imbibition
- Preserve dermis

### Meshing

**Purpose:**
- Expand graft
- Allows drainage
- Contours to irregular surfaces

**Ratios:**
- 1:1 (no expansion, drainage only)
- 1:1.5 (50% expansion)
- 1:3 (200% expansion)
- 1:4+ (burns, large areas)

**Disadvantage:**
- Visible mesh pattern
- More contraction
- Avoid on face

### Donor Site Care

**STSG Donor:**
- Occlusive dressing
- Moist healing
- Heals 7-14 days
- May use NPWT

**FTSG Donor:**
- Primary closure
- Remove sutures 7-10 days`,
