        id: 'peel-1',
        title: 'Peel Depth and Classification',
        content: `## Chemical Peel Fundamentals

### Definition

**Chemical Peel:**
- Controlled chemical injury
- Induces exfoliation
- Stimulates regeneration
- Skin rejuvenation

### Depth Classification

**Superficial (Epidermis):**
- Stratum corneum to papillary dermis
- Minimal downtime
- Multiple treatments needed
- Mild improvement

**Medium (Papillary Dermis):**
- Through papillary dermis
- 7-14 days recovery
- More significant results
- Some risk of scarring

**Deep (Reticular Dermis):**
- Into reticular dermis
- 2-3 weeks+ recovery
- Dramatic results
- Highest risk

### Glogau Classification

**Photoaging Scale:**
| Type | Age | Wrinkles | Description |
|------|-----|----------|-------------|
| I | 20-30s | Mild | No makeup needed |
| II | 30-40s | Moderate | Some makeup |
| III | 50+ | Advanced | Always wears makeup |
| IV | 60-70s | Severe | Can't wear makeup |

### Fitzpatrick Skin Types

| Type | Characteristics | Peel Risk |
|------|-----------------|-----------|
| I | Always burns | Low |
| II | Usually burns | Low |
| III | Sometimes burns | Moderate |
| IV | Rarely burns | Higher |
| V | Very rarely burns | High |
| VI | Never burns | Highest |

### Indications

**Superficial:**
- Mild photodamage
- Acne
- Melasma
- Rough texture

**Medium:**
- Moderate wrinkles
- Actinic keratoses
- Pigment irregularities

**Deep:**
- Severe photodamage
- Deep wrinkles
- Acne scarring`,
