        id: 'peel-2',
        title: 'Superficial and Medium Depth Agents',
        content: `## Peeling Agents

### Superficial Agents

**Alpha Hydroxy Acids (AHA):**
- Glycolic acid (most common)
- Lactic acid
- 20-70% concentration
- Neutralize with water or bicarbonate

**Jessner's Solution:**
- Resorcinol + salicylic acid + lactic acid
- Self-limiting depth
- Can combine with other agents

**Salicylic Acid:**
- Beta hydroxy acid (BHA)
- Lipophilic (good for acne)
- Self-neutralizing (precipitates)
- 20-30% concentration

**TCA (Low):**
- 10-20% TCA
- Superficial depth
- Frosting indicates neutralization

### Medium Depth Agents

**TCA 35-50%:**
- Papillary dermis
- White frosting endpoint
- Self-neutralizing

**Combination (Monheit):**
- Jessner's + 35% TCA
- Better penetration
- More even depth

**88% Phenol:**
- Medium depth without occlusion
- Rarely used alone

### TCA Frosting Levels

| Level | Appearance | Depth |
|-------|------------|-------|
| 1 | Erythema with streaks | Superficial |
| 2 | White coat, pink through | Papillary dermis |
| 3 | Solid white | Deep papillary |

### Application Technique

**Principles:**
- Degrease skin first
- Even application
- Watch for frosting
- Neutralize if needed (glycolic)
- Multiple passes increase depth`,
