        content: `## Infantile Hemangioma Basics

### Definition

**Infantile Hemangioma (IH):**
- Most common tumor of infancy
- Benign vascular tumor
- GLUT-1 positive (diagnostic)
- Characteristic growth pattern

### Epidemiology

**Incidence:**
- 4-5% of infants
- 10-12% of premature infants

**Risk Factors:**
- Female (3:1)
- Caucasian
- Premature/low birth weight
- Multiple gestation
- Advanced maternal age

### Natural History

**Phases:**
| Phase | Timing | Characteristics |
|-------|--------|-----------------|
| Proliferative | 0-9 months | Rapid growth |
| Plateau | 9-12 months | Stable |
| Involution | 1-7 years | Gradual shrinking |

**Growth Pattern:**
- Not usually present at birth
- Appears first weeks of life
- 80% of growth by 3-5 months
- Involutes over years

### Classification by Depth

**Superficial:**
- Bright red ("strawberry")
- Papular surface
- Best involution

**Deep:**
- Bluish hue
- Subcutaneous mass
- Skin may be normal

**Mixed:**
- Both components
- Most common type

### GLUT-1

**Glucose Transporter-1:**
- Positive in ALL infantile hemangiomas
- Differentiates from other vascular tumors
- Remains positive even after involution
- Key diagnostic marker`,
