        id: 'syn-1',
        title: 'Classification',
        content: `## Syndactyly Classification

### Definition

**Syndactyly:**
- Failure of digital separation
- Most common hand malformation
- Occurs 1:2000-3000 births

### Classification

**By Extent:**
| Type | Description |
|------|-------------|
| Complete | Extends to fingertip |
| Incomplete | Doesn't reach fingertip |

**By Depth:**
| Type | Description |
|------|-------------|
| Simple | Skin/soft tissue only |
| Complex | Bone/nail involvement |
| Complicated | Accessory bones, abnormal bones |

### Most Common

**Simple Complete:**
- Web 3 (middle-ring) most common
- Often bilateral
- Familial pattern

### Associated Conditions

**Syndromes:**
| Syndrome | Features |
|----------|----------|
| Poland | Chest wall + hand (symbrachydactyly) |
| Apert | Multiple syndactyly, midface hypoplasia |
| Constrictive band | Ring constrictions, amputations |

**Apert Syndrome:**
- Craniosynostosis
- Bilateral complex syndactyly
- "Spade hand" or "mitten hand"
- Bone synostoses

### Anatomy

**Normal Web Space:**
- Web commissure at level of MCP heads
- 45° slope
- Allows finger abduction

**Abnormal Features:**
- Proximal web position
- Shared nail (complex)
- Bifurcating vessels/nerves
- May share structures`,
