        id: 'abx-1',
        title: 'Antibiotic Prophylaxis: Core Principles',
        content: `# Antibiotic Prophylaxis in Plastic Surgery

## Fundamental Principles

### Goals of Prophylaxis
- **Prevent surgical site infection (SSI)**
- Reduce wound complications
- NOT treat existing infection
- NOT sterilize the wound

### Key Timing Principles

| Timing | Recommendation |
|--------|----------------|
| **Before Incision** | Within 60 minutes (optimal 30 min) |
| **Vancomycin/Fluoroquinolones** | Start 120 minutes before |
| **Redosing** | Every 2 half-lives during surgery |
| **Duration** | ≤24 hours post-op (most cases) |

### Clean Surgery Classification

**Class I (Clean):**
- No infection present
- No GI/GU/respiratory entry
- Primary closure
- SSI rate: 1-2%

**Class II (Clean-Contaminated):**
- Controlled entry into tract
- Minor breaks in technique
- SSI rate: 3-11%

### When Prophylaxis is Indicated

**ALWAYS indicated:**
- Implant/prosthetic placement
- Procedures >3 hours
- Major flap surgery
- Immunocompromised patients

**Consider based on risk:**
- Clean surgery without implants
- Short procedures
- Low-risk patients`,
