        title: 'VTE Risk Assessment in Plastic Surgery',
        content: `# Venous Thromboembolism Risk Assessment

## The Problem

### VTE in Plastic Surgery
- DVT incidence: 0.3-1.1% in cosmetic surgery
- PE incidence: 0.03-0.3%
- Fatal PE: Leading cause of death in cosmetic surgery
- **Preventable with appropriate prophylaxis**

### Why Plastic Surgery Patients Are At Risk

**Procedure Factors:**
- Prolonged operative time
- Patient positioning (prone, lateral)
- Tissue manipulation and inflammation
- Immobilization postoperatively

**Patient Factors:**
- Often elective (can optimize)
- May have multiple comorbidities
- Combined procedures common
- Obesity in body contouring

## Caprini Risk Assessment Model

### Risk Scoring System

| Points | Risk Factors |
|--------|--------------|
| **1 point each** | Age 41-60, minor surgery, BMI >25, swollen legs, varicose veins, pregnancy/postpartum, history unexplained stillbirth, oral contraceptives/HRT, sepsis <1 month, serious lung disease, abnormal pulmonary function, acute MI, CHF <1 month, IBD, immobility |
| **2 points each** | Age 61-74, arthroscopic surgery, major open surgery >45min, laparoscopic surgery >45min, malignancy, confined to bed >72h, immobilizing plaster cast, central venous access |
| **3 points each** | Age >75, history of DVT/PE, family history DVT/PE, Factor V Leiden, prothrombin mutation, lupus anticoagulant, anticardiolipin antibodies, elevated homocysteine, HIT, other congenital/acquired thrombophilia |
| **5 points** | Stroke <1 month, elective arthroplasty, hip/pelvis/leg fracture, acute spinal cord injury <1 month |

### Risk Categories

| Score | Risk Level | DVT Risk | Recommendation |
|-------|------------|----------|----------------|
| 0-1 | Very Low | <0.5% | Early ambulation |
| 2 | Low | 1.5% | Mechanical prophylaxis |
| 3-4 | Moderate | 3% | Mechanical +/- pharmacologic |
| ≥5 | High | 6%+ | Mechanical + pharmacologic |

### Plastic Surgery Specific Risk Factors

**High-Risk Procedures:**
- Abdominoplasty (especially with liposuction)
- Body contouring after weight loss
- Free flap reconstruction
- Combined procedures >4 hours
- Prone positioning`,
