        id: 'preop-opt-3',
        title: 'Preoperative Testing Guidelines',
        content: `# Evidence-Based Preoperative Testing

## Testing Philosophy

**Key Principle:** Test only when results will change management

**NOT indicated:**
- Routine testing for healthy patients
- "Just to have a baseline"
- Testing without clinical indication

## Test Indications

### Complete Blood Count (CBC)

**Indicated:**
| Indication | Reasoning |
|------------|-----------|
| Known anemia | Baseline, may need optimization |
| Chronic disease (renal, liver) | Anemia common |
| Bleeding disorder history | Baseline |
| Major surgery (expected blood loss) | Transfusion planning |
| Age >65 with comorbidities | Screen for occult disease |

**NOT indicated:** Routine for healthy patients undergoing low-blood-loss procedures

### Metabolic Panel (BMP/CMP)

**Indicated:**
| Indication | Reasoning |
|------------|-----------|
| Diabetes | Glucose, renal function |
| Hypertension | Electrolytes, renal function |
| Diuretic/ACE-I/ARB use | Electrolytes, renal function |
| Renal disease | Baseline, medication dosing |
| Liver disease | Hepatic function |

### Coagulation Studies (PT/INR, PTT)

**Indicated:**
| Indication | Reasoning |
|------------|-----------|
| Anticoagulant therapy | Baseline, reversal planning |
| Liver disease | Synthetic function |
| Bleeding history | Screen for coagulopathy |
| Malnutrition | Vitamin K deficiency |

**NOT indicated:** Routine screening; history more sensitive

### Pregnancy Test

**Indicated:**
- All women of childbearing potential
- Day of surgery testing
- Mandatory before anesthesia

### Urinalysis

**Indicated:**
- Urologic procedures
- Implant surgery (some protocols)
- Symptoms of UTI

**NOT indicated:** Routine screening

### Electrocardiogram (ECG)

**Indicated:**
| Indication | Age/Condition |
|------------|---------------|
| Known cardiac disease | All patients |
| Cardiovascular symptoms | All patients |
| Diabetes | Consider if other risk factors |
| Age alone | Generally NOT indicated |
| High-risk surgery | Consider if risk factors |

### Chest X-Ray

**Indicated:**
- New or worsening respiratory symptoms
- Known significant pulmonary disease
- Cardiac disease with possible pulmonary involvement

**NOT indicated:**
- Routine preoperative screening
- Age alone
- Stable chronic pulmonary disease

## Testing by Procedure Risk

### Minimal-Risk Procedures
(Blepharoplasty, minor excisions)

| Test | Indication |
|------|------------|
| Any testing | Based on comorbidities only |
| Pregnancy test | All reproductive-age women |

### Low-Risk Procedures
(Rhinoplasty, facelift, breast augmentation)

| Test | Indication |
|------|------------|
| CBC | If expected blood loss or anemia |
| BMP | If diabetes, hypertension, on diuretics |
| Coags | Only if bleeding history/anticoagulants |
| ECG | Only if cardiac history |

### Moderate-Risk Procedures
(Abdominoplasty, breast reconstruction)

| Test | Indication |
|------|------------|
| CBC | All patients |
| BMP | All patients with comorbidities |
| Coags | If indicated by history/meds |
| ECG | If cardiac risk factors |
| Type and screen | If significant blood loss expected |`,
