        content: `# Specialty Consultation and Summary

## Cardiac Clearance

### When to Obtain

**Required:**
- Active cardiac conditions
- Poor functional capacity (<4 METs) + risk factors
- High-risk surgery with cardiac history

**Not Needed:**
- Stable cardiac disease
- Good functional capacity (>4 METs)
- Low-risk procedures

### Active Cardiac Conditions

| Condition | Action |
|-----------|--------|
| Unstable angina | Delay surgery, cardiology |
| Recent MI (<60 days) | Delay elective surgery |
| Decompensated HF | Optimize before surgery |
| Significant arrhythmia | Evaluate and treat |
| Severe valvular disease | Cardiology evaluation |

### What to Ask Cardiology

❌ "Clear for surgery" (inappropriate)
✓ "Assessment of cardiac risk and optimization recommendations"

## Pulmonary Clearance

### When to Obtain

| Indication | Action |
|------------|--------|
| Severe COPD | Optimization, pulmonary toilet |
| Uncontrolled asthma | Optimize control |
| Severe OSA | CPAP compliance, anesthesia planning |
| Recent URI | May delay 2-4 weeks |

### Obstructive Sleep Apnea (OSA)

**STOP-BANG Screening:**
| Factor | Point |
|--------|-------|
| Snoring | 1 |
| Tiredness | 1 |
| Observed apnea | 1 |
| High blood Pressure | 1 |
| BMI >35 | 1 |
| Age >50 | 1 |
| Neck circumference >40cm | 1 |
| Male Gender | 1 |

**Score ≥5:** High risk for moderate-severe OSA

**Perioperative Considerations:**
- CPAP compliance preoperatively
- Monitoring postoperatively
- Opioid sensitivity
- Consider overnight observation

## Preoperative Optimization Checklist

### 4+ Weeks Before Surgery

□ Smoking cessation initiated
□ Diabetes optimization (HbA1c check)
□ Nutrition assessment/supplementation
□ Stop OCP/HRT (if indicated)
□ Specialty consultations obtained

### 2 Weeks Before Surgery

□ Stop herbal supplements
□ Confirm medication adjustments
□ Verify smoking cessation
□ Review test results
□ Confirm procedure plan

### Day Before Surgery

□ NPO instructions confirmed
□ Medication instructions clear
□ Transportation arranged
□ Responsible adult escort confirmed
□ Preoperative instructions reviewed

### Day of Surgery

□ NPO status verified
□ Prescribed meds taken appropriately
□ Glucose checked (diabetics)
□ Pregnancy test (if indicated)
□ Consent signed
□ Prophylaxis ordered (VTE, antibiotics)

## Quick Reference Summary

### Always Optimize Before Elective Surgery

| Factor | Target |
|--------|--------|
| Smoking | Cessation ≥4 weeks |
| HbA1c | <8% (ideally <7.5%) |
| BMI | <35 preferred for cosmetic |
| Albumin | >3.0 g/dL |
| Anemia | Hgb >10 (ideally >12) |
| Blood pressure | Well controlled |

### Cannot Operate Until

- Active cardiac condition resolved
- Glucose consistently >300
- Active infection treated
- Pregnancy test positive (unless obstetric)
- Patient understanding and consent inadequate

### Document in Chart

1. Preoperative risk assessment
2. Optimization measures taken
3. Tests and results
4. Consultations and recommendations
5. Informed consent discussion`,
