        content: `# Perioperative Anaphylaxis

## Recognition

| System | Signs |
|--------|-------|
| Skin | Urticaria, flushing |
| Respiratory | Bronchospasm, stridor |
| Cardiovascular | Hypotension, tachycardia |
| GI | Nausea, vomiting |

### Common Triggers
- Antibiotics
- Latex
- Muscle relaxants
- Blood products

## Treatment

### EPINEPHRINE - Primary Treatment

| Route | Dose |
|-------|------|
| IM (mild-mod) | 0.3-0.5 mg |
| IV (severe) | 10-100 mcg |
| IV infusion | 1-4 mcg/min |

### Additional
- IV fluids 1-2L bolus
- Albuterol for bronchospasm
- Diphenhydramine 25-50mg
- Methylprednisolone 125mg`,
