        id: 'flap-mon-1',
        title: 'Flap Monitoring Fundamentals',
        content: `# Flap Monitoring Essentials

## Why Monitoring Matters

### Critical Window
- Most flap failures occur in first 24-72 hours
- Early detection = salvage opportunity
- Delayed recognition = flap loss

### Salvage Rates
| Detection Time | Salvage Rate |
|----------------|--------------|
| <6 hours | >80% |
| 6-12 hours | 50-70% |
| >12 hours | <30% |

## Monitoring Frequency

### Free Flaps
| Time Period | Frequency |
|-------------|-----------|
| 0-24 hours | Every 1 hour |
| 24-48 hours | Every 2 hours |
| 48-72 hours | Every 4 hours |
| After 72 hours | Every 8 hours |

### Pedicled Flaps
| Time Period | Frequency |
|-------------|-----------|
| 0-24 hours | Every 2-4 hours |
| 24-72 hours | Every 4-6 hours |
| After 72 hours | Every 8 hours |

## Clinical Assessment Parameters

### The 5 Cs of Flap Monitoring

| Parameter | Normal | Concern |
|-----------|--------|---------|
| **Color** | Pink, similar to surrounding | Pale (arterial) or dusky (venous) |
| **Capillary refill** | 1-2 seconds | >3 sec (arterial) or <1 sec (venous) |
| **Consistency** | Soft, supple | Turgid (venous) or flaccid (arterial) |
| **Contour** | Stable | Swelling (venous congestion) |
| **Coolness** | Warm to touch | Cold (arterial insufficiency) |`,
