        id: 'flap-mon-4',
        title: 'Emergency Response and Summary',
        content: `# Flap Emergency Response

## When to Call Surgeon

### IMMEDIATE Notification
- Any change in color (pale or dusky)
- Change in capillary refill
- Temperature change
- Loss of Doppler signal
- Increased swelling

### Response Checklist
□ Call surgeon immediately
□ Remove all dressings
□ Release tight sutures if ordered
□ Check patient position
□ Document findings
□ Optimize patient (BP, temp, hydration)

## Surgical Response

### Arterial Problem
- Return to OR for exploration
- Identify and correct cause
- May need revision or thrombectomy
- Consider anticoagulation

### Venous Problem
- Release any compression
- Consider leeches as temporizing measure
- Return to OR for exploration
- May need venous revision

## Leech Therapy

### Indications
- Venous congestion
- Temporizing until OR
- Adjunct post-revision

### Protocol
| Aspect | Guideline |
|--------|-----------|
| Apply | To congested area |
| Duration | Until detaches (20-60 min) |
| Reapply | Every 1-2 hours as needed |
| Antibiotics | Cipro/Bactrim coverage |
| Blood | Monitor Hgb (bleeding) |

## Quick Reference Summary

### Monitoring Schedule
| Period | Free Flap | Pedicled |
|--------|-----------|----------|
| 0-24h | q1h | q2-4h |
| 24-48h | q2h | q4-6h |
| 48-72h | q4h | q6-8h |

### Normal vs Abnormal

| Parameter | Normal | Action |
|-----------|--------|--------|
| Color | Pink | Document |
| Cap refill | 1-2 sec | Document |
| Temp | Warm | Document |
| Doppler | Present | Document |
| ANY change | - | CALL NOW |

### Documentation
- Time of check
- All parameters assessed
- Comparison to baseline
- Any concerns and actions taken`,
