        content: `# WHO Surgical Safety Checklist

## Three Phases

### Sign In (Before Induction)
□ Patient identity confirmed
□ Procedure and site confirmed
□ Site marked
□ Consent signed
□ Anesthesia safety check complete
□ Pulse oximeter functioning
□ Known allergies documented
□ Difficult airway/aspiration risk assessed
□ Blood loss risk assessed

### Time Out (Before Incision)
□ All team members introduced
□ Patient identity confirmed
□ Procedure confirmed
□ Site confirmed
□ Antibiotic prophylaxis given
□ Anticipated critical events reviewed:
  - Surgeon: Key steps, duration, blood loss
  - Anesthesia: Patient concerns
  - Nursing: Equipment ready, sterility confirmed
□ Imaging displayed (if required)

### Sign Out (Before Leaving OR)
□ Procedure name recorded
□ Instrument/sponge counts correct
□ Specimens labeled
□ Equipment problems documented
□ Recovery concerns identified

## Implementation

### Key Principles
| Principle | Action |
|-----------|--------|
| Team participation | Everyone speaks |
| Verbal confirmation | Out loud responses |
| No hierarchy | Anyone can stop |
| Documentation | Record completion |`,
