        id: 'safety-2',
        title: 'Wrong Site Surgery Prevention',
        content: `# Wrong Site Surgery Prevention

## Universal Protocol

### Preoperative Verification
| Step | Verification |
|------|--------------|
| At scheduling | Procedure and site |
| At admission | Consent matches schedule |
| Before transport | Site marking verified |
| In holding area | Final verification |

### Site Marking
**Requirements:**
- Marked by operating surgeon
- With patient awake/involved
- At or near incision site
- Unambiguous mark (initials, YES)
- Must be visible after prep/drape

**Marking Method:**
- Use permanent marker
- Mark with initials or YES
- Dont mark non-operative site
- Mark laterality clearly

### Final Verification (Time Out)
- Active communication
- All team members participate
- Confirm:
  - Correct patient
  - Correct procedure
  - Correct site
  - Correct position
  - Correct implants/equipment

## High-Risk Situations

### Increased Risk
| Situation | Mitigation |
|-----------|------------|
| Multiple procedures | Mark each site |
| Multiple surgeons | Clear communication |
| Emergency | Abbreviated but complete |
| Pediatric | Parent involvement |
| Language barrier | Interpreter |

## If Wrong Site Identified

### STOP Immediately
1. Do not proceed
2. Assess what happened
3. Correct course if possible
4. Document thoroughly
5. Report through proper channels
6. Disclose to patient`,
