        id: 'safety-4',
        title: 'Complication Disclosure',
        content: `# Complication Disclosure

## Ethical Obligation

### Why Disclose
- Ethical duty to patient
- Builds trust
- Legal protection (in many states)
- Opportunity to apologize
- Enables appropriate care

### When to Disclose
| Situation | Timing |
|-----------|--------|
| Adverse event | As soon as practical |
| Unexpected outcome | When identified |
| Error | Immediately when safe |

## How to Disclose

### SPIKES Protocol

| Step | Action |
|------|--------|
| **S**etting | Private, comfortable, support present |
| **P**erception | What does patient understand? |
| **I**nvitation | Ask permission to discuss |
| **K**nowledge | Share facts clearly |
| **E**motions | Address feelings with empathy |
| **S**trategy | Next steps, follow-up plan |

### Key Principles
- Be honest and direct
- Express empathy/concern
- Avoid blame
- Explain what happened
- Explain what will be done
- Allow questions
- Provide follow-up plan

### What to Say

**Do:**
- I am sorry this happened
- Here is what occurred...
- This is what we are doing...
- I will continue to care for you

**Dont:**
- This wasnt my fault
- This never happens
- You should have...
- Defensive language

## Documentation

### Medical Record
- Factual description of event
- Actions taken
- Patient notification documented
- Follow-up plan
- Do NOT document blame/fault

### Incident Report
- Complete institutional forms
- Report to risk management
- Report to quality committee
- Separate from medical record`,
