        content: `# Patient Selection Criteria

## Appropriate Candidates

### Medical Criteria
| Factor | Criteria |
|--------|----------|
| ASA Class | I-II ideal; III stable acceptable |
| BMI | <40 preferred; facility dependent |
| Age | No absolute limit; functional status |
| Comorbidities | Well controlled |
| Medications | Managed appropriately |

### Social Criteria
| Requirement | Detail |
|-------------|--------|
| Escort | Responsible adult required |
| Supervision | 24-hour adult care at home |
| Distance | Reasonable from care |
| Phone | Access for follow-up |
| Instructions | Ability to follow |

## Patient Selection Tool

### Consider Inpatient If:
□ ASA III with unstable conditions
□ BMI >40 (facility dependent)
□ Severe OSA requiring CPAP
□ Insulin-dependent diabetes, poorly controlled
□ Significant cardiac/pulmonary disease
□ Anticoagulation that cannot be held
□ Unreliable social support
□ Procedure >6 hours anticipated

### Procedure Considerations
| Factor | Limit |
|--------|-------|
| Expected duration | Generally <6 hours |
| Blood loss | <500 mL expected |
| Recovery | Able to ambulate |
| Pain control | Manageable with oral meds |
| Postop care | No specialized needs |

## Preoperative Preparation

### Patient Instructions
- NPO guidelines (clear liquids 2h, solids 6-8h)
- Medication instructions
- What to bring
- What to wear
- Arrival time
- Escort requirements`,
