        id: 'photo-1',
        title: 'Photography Standards',
        content: `# Medical Photography Standards

## Purpose of Medical Photography

### Uses
| Purpose | Application |
|---------|-------------|
| Documentation | Pre/postoperative record |
| Treatment planning | Surgical planning |
| Patient education | Explain procedure |
| Outcomes assessment | Track results |
| Teaching | Education |
| Publication | Research, textbooks |
| Marketing | With consent |

## Standardization

### Consistent Elements
| Element | Standard |
|---------|----------|
| Background | Neutral (blue, gray, black) |
| Lighting | Consistent, even |
| Distance | Standardized for body part |
| Position | Reproducible poses |
| Camera settings | Consistent |
| Timing | Pre, intra, post at intervals |

### Views by Body Region

**Face:**
- Frontal
- Right and left oblique (45°)
- Right and left lateral (90°)
- Submental/base view

**Breast:**
- Frontal (arms at sides and raised)
- Right and left oblique
- Right and left lateral

**Abdomen:**
- Frontal
- Right and left oblique
- Right and left lateral

## Technical Considerations

### Camera Equipment
| Element | Consideration |
|---------|---------------|
| Camera | DSLR or quality mirrorless |
| Lens | Standard or macro |
| Flash | Ring flash or dual flash |
| Tripod | For consistency |

### Settings
- Manual mode for consistency
- Appropriate white balance
- Adequate depth of field
- Resolution appropriate for use`,
